        {
          "attributes": {
            "definition": {
              "text": "### Shared investigation\n\n1. Identify the affected survey from the monitor: CSAT uses `beaver-survey-enhancer`; NPS uses `beaver-nps`.\n2. Confirm the affected CronJob exists, is not suspended, and is still scheduled every five minutes.\n3. Check `lastScheduleTime` and whether recent Jobs succeeded, failed, or remained active. If the schedule was intentionally reduced, revise the heartbeat monitor windows.\n4. Inspect Job and pod events for pending or unschedulable pods, cluster capacity, quotas, image pulls, missing secrets, permissions, crashes, and missed starting deadlines.\n5. If the process started, inspect PostgreSQL connectivity, fetching unenhanced submissions, Vertex calls, persistence, and execution duration.\n6. If Jobs succeeded but the heartbeat is absent, verify the deployed Beaver version, StatsD configuration, Datadog Agent connectivity, metric name, `kube_namespace`, and `survey_type` tags.\n7. During migration, compare the new heartbeat with the matching legacy counter.\n8. Do not investigate missing customer submissions as the cause. A healthy job with no work emits `result:empty`.",
              "type": "markdown"
            }
          },
          "id": "3mpudflu",
          "type": "notebook_cells"
        },
        {
          "attributes": {
            "definition": {
              "text": "### Signal interpretation\n\n| Kubernetes Jobs | Enhancer heartbeat | Likely meaning |\n|---|---|---|\n| Missing | Missing | CronJob scheduling or Kubernetes control-plane problem |\n| Failed | Missing | Job startup or execution failure |\n| Successful | Missing | Metric emission, Datadog Agent, or deployed-version problem |\n| Successful | Present | Healthy or recovered |",
              "type": "markdown"
            }
          },
          "id": "99m34skd",
          "type": "notebook_cells"
        },
        {
          "attributes": {
            "definition": {
              "text": "### Recovery criteria\n\nRecovery requires all of the following for the affected survey:\n\n1. A new Job completes successfully.\n2. A new `beaver.survey.enhancer_run.count` point appears with the expected `survey_type`.\n3. The result may be `empty` or `success`.\n4. The heartbeat monitor returns to `OK`.\n5. The next scheduled execution also completes normally.\n\n### Migration note\n\nRemove the legacy heartbeat cell after the new metric has been present in production for at least one week, agrees with Kubernetes Job success for both CronJobs, and all heartbeat monitors have been validated.",
              "type": "markdown"
            }
          },
          "id": "qd5mj9v1",
          "type": "notebook_cells"
        }
